WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.620
Read these two words.

2
00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:02.580
The.

3
00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:03.470
Cat.

4
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.460
Easy.

5
00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:06.840
Now look closely at the middle letters.

6
00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:10.110
Slide them out and lay
one on top of the other.

7
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.480
They match exactly.

8
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.030
It's the same shape.

9
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.630
So why did you read it
as an H in one word,

10
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.480
and an A in the other?

11
00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:21.340
In this mission, you'll see how the same
stimulus can be perceived differently

12
00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:25.200
by different people, or
by you at different times.

13
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:30.740
You'll meet perceptual set: a readiness
to perceive certain things and not others.

14
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:34.630
It's why, when you're hungry,
food signs jump out at you.

15
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:39.650
Your mission: work out what decides
whether that one shape becomes an H or an

16
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:40.200
A.
